<style is:global>.research,.prototype{padding:105px 5.5vw;background:#d8d5cc}.research{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.15fr;gap:8vw;align-items:end}.research video{width:100%;height:450px;object-fit:cover;background:#111}.spot-cooling{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;align-items:center;background:#151614;color:#f5f4ef}.spot-cooling>img{display:block;width:100%;height:610px;object-fit:cover}.spot-cooling>div{padding:70px 7vw;max-width:560px}.spot-cooling h2{margin:24px 0 0;font-size:clamp(48px,5.8vw,86px);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.075em;line-height:.88}.spot-cooling p:last-of-type{margin:26px 0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.5}.spot-cooling div img{width:100%;height:190px;object-fit:cover}.prototype{background:#f7f6f1}.prototype-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:9px;margin-top:55px}.prototype-grid .image-button{aspect-ratio:4/3}.prototype-grid .image-button:first-child{grid-column:span 2;grid-row:span 2;aspect-ratio:auto}.prototype-grid .image-button:first-child img{height:100%}@media(max-width:760px){.research,.prototype{display:block;padding:72px 20px}.research video{height:270px;margin-top:38px}.spot-cooling{display:flex;flex-direction:column}.spot-cooling>img{height:330px}.spot-cooling>div{padding:66px 20px}.spot-cooling h2{font-size:49px}.spot-cooling p:last-of-type{font-size:16px}.spot-cooling div img{height:170px}.prototype-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:6px;margin-top:38px}.prototype-grid .image-button:first-child{grid-column:span 2;grid-row:auto;aspect-ratio:16/10}.prototype-grid .image-button:first-child img{height:100%}}</style>
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>AERO — Ryan Antonius</title></head><body><header><a href="/">RYAN ANTONIUS</a><nav><a href="/industrial">WORK</a><a href="/#contact">CONTACT</a><a href="/about">ABOUT</a></nav></header><main>
<section class="hero"><img src={media('97a2bb_a9562acfd236415cb1cb186d930a02f2~mv2.gif')} alt="AERO cooling accessory animation"/><div class="hero-copy"><p>PERSONAL COOLING · PRODUCT DESIGN</p><h1>AERO</h1><span>2017</span></div></section>
<section class="overview"><div><p class="label">PROJECT OVERVIEW</p><h2>Relief,<br/>without the interruption.</h2></div><div class="overview-copy"><p>AERO is a portable cooling accessory for commuters. It directs cooling at the neck, making relief immediate and less intrusive than a handheld fan.</p><dl><div><dt>SERVICE</dt><dd>Product design</dd></div><div><dt>YEAR</dt><dd>2017</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<section class="research"><div class="section-heading"><p class="label">01 · RESEARCH</p><h2>Heat stress starts before the destination.</h2><p>Urban areas become warmer when natural cover is replaced by buildings and infrastructure that retain heat and restrict wind flow. The result is a commute that can quickly become physically stressful.</p></div><video autoplay muted loop playsinline><source src="https://video.wixstatic.com/video/97a2bb_21c1322a9f6845fa9a733eee4cf66bb6/1080p/mp4/file.mp4" type="video/mp4"/></video></section>
<section class="development"><div class="section-heading"><p class="label">02 · DESIGN DEVELOPMENT</p><h2>Shape meets airflow.</h2></div><div class="render-grid">{renders.map((image)=><button class="image-button" data-image={image}><img src={image} alt="AERO design development"/></button>)}</div></section>
<section class="spot-cooling"><img src={media('97a2bb_0e77cb08e155429cb57b009142c54303~mv2.jpg')} alt="AERO spot-cooling study"/><div><p class="label">03 · SPOT COOLING</p><h2>Cool the pulse points.</h2><p>AERO targets the neck, where blood vessels sit close to the skin. Cooling this area supports the body’s natural evaporation process and offers a practical place for fast, hands-free relief.</p></div></section>
<section class="prototype"><div class="section-heading"><p class="label">04 · FUNCTIONAL PROTOTYPE</p><h2>Designed to be made and worn.</h2><p>A functional prototype brought the electronics—battery, motor and airflow system—into a 3D-printed housing. The orange parts show the object moving from concept to a working wearable.</p></div><div class="prototype-grid">{prototypeImages.map((image)=><button class="image-button" data-image={image}><img src={image} alt="AERO orange functional prototype"/></button>)}</div></section>
<section class="project-navigation"><a href="/industrial">← ALL INDUSTRIAL DESIGN</a><a href="/industrial/qiq-mobility"><span>NEXT PROJECT</span><strong>QIQ Mobility →</strong></a></section></main><footer>RYAN ANTONIUS © 2026</footer><dialog id="lightbox"><button class="close" aria-label="Close image">×</button><img alt="Expanded AERO image"/><button class="previous" aria-label="Previous image">←</button><button class="next" aria-label="Next image">→</button></dialog><script>const modal=document.querySelector('#lightbox'),large=modal?.querySelector('img');let active=0,activeGallery,touchX=0,touchY=0;const items=()=>activeGallery?[...activeGallery.querySelectorAll('.image-button')]:[];const show=(step=0)=>{const list=items();if(!list.length)return;active=(active+step+list.length)%list.length;if(large)large.src=list[active]?.dataset.image||''};document.querySelectorAll('.image-button').forEach(item=>item.addEventListener('click',()=>{activeGallery=item.closest('section');const list=items();active=list.indexOf(item);show();modal?.showModal()}));document.querySelector('.close')?.addEventListener('click',()=>modal?.close());document.querySelector('.previous')?.addEventListener('click',()=>show(-1));document.querySelector('.next')?.addEventListener('click',()=>show(1));document.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(!modal?.open)return;if(event.key==='ArrowLeft')show(-1);if(event.key==='ArrowRight')show(1);if(event.key==='Escape')modal.close()});modal?.addEventListener('touchstart',event=>{const touch=event.changedTouches[0];touchX=touch.clientX;touchY=touch.clientY},{passive:true});modal?.addEventListener('touchend',event=>{const touch=event.changedTouches[0],deltaX=touch.clientX-touchX,deltaY=touch.clientY-touchY;if(Math.abs(deltaX)>48&&Math.abs(deltaX)>Math.abs(deltaY))show(deltaX<0?1:-1)},{passive:true});</script></body></html>
